  "solution_principle": "1- Translation aka Move:\r\n\r\n- Construct a Point.\r\n\r\n- Type \"Move\" and use its component.\r\n\r\n- Type \"X\" and choose \"Unit X\". So the same for \"Y\" and \"Z\".\r\nThese are the basic vector directions.\r\n\r\n- The INPUT of these basic vectors can used to determine their factor, or length...\r\n\r\n- However, sometimes vectors don't have this option available, such as the \"Vector XYZ\" and \"Vector 2pt\"\r\nTherefore, the \"Amplitude\" component works as the factor, or length. The \"Amplitude\" component needs two INPUTS:\r\n1- Vector\r\n2- Numerical value (to give a length to the vector).",
